algorithms.pseudocode:
Algorithm: ClosureCompress(cl, len, x)
  Input: idempotent closure cl, length function len, data object x
  Output: canonical representative cl(x), which minimizes len in [x]_cl
  1. Compute y ← cl(x)           // O(T_cl)
  2. Return y                      // y is the shortest representative
  // Correctness: By Theorem 1, len(y) ≤ len(z) for all z with cl(z) = cl(x)
  // By Theorem 2, len(y) = MDL within closure class
  // By Theorem 4 (one-step): cl(y) = y, so no further iteration needed

Algorithm: TropicalNormalize(x)
  Input: vector x ∈ ℝⁿ
  Output: canonical representative with min coordinate = 0
  1. m ← min(x₁, ..., xₙ)       // O(n)
  2. For i = 1 to n:               // O(n)
       yᵢ ← xᵢ - m
  3. Return y
  // Properties: idempotent, translation-invariant
  // min(y) = 0, sum(y) = sum(x) - n·m
  // Total: O(n) time, O(n) space
